          "sourcePage": 22,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 10, upper-right graph",
          "description": "Qualitative displacement–time curve with six labelled time ticks, a shallow first maximum slightly before t₁, a negative minimum near t₃ and the highest positive maximum near t₅. The curve crosses at t₂ and t₄ and its descending arrowhead meets the axis near t₆. Both axes have arrowheads at both ends. No numerical scale or grid is supplied.",
          "mathematics": "Origins correspond to zero displacement; rest corresponds to horizontal tangents; distance from the origin is the magnitude of displacement.",
